    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d371">

                <pb facs="0562" n="515" xml:id="pg515"/>

                <head>371. Telegram 1219 to Geneva<anchor n="1" xml:id="d371-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName>Washington</placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1955-11-12">November 12, 1955, 1:03
                            p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <pb facs="d371-1" n="1" type="facsimile" xml:id="d371-1"/>
                <p>1219. For Johnson.</p>
                <p>Re your 1135, para. 25, <hi rendition="#italic">N.Y. Times</hi> article November
                    8 could not RPT not have been based on any responsible U.S. official source. We
                    have no indication as to origin, although internal evidence points strongly to
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Daily Worker</hi> article as chief inspiration.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#bold">Hoover</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d371-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d371-f1-content">
                <p>Source: Department of State, Central Files, 611.93/11–1055. Secret; Limit
                    Distribution. Drafted by McConaughy; cleared in draft by Sebald.</p>
            </note>
